# AA2.0 Microsoft Fabric ETL — Cursor AI Rules

## Project Context
- Project: Census Analytics 2.0 (AA2.0)
- Company: Ascensus / Persistent Systems
- Team: DataOps / DI&T
- Developer: Pavan Annachedu

## Architecture Constraints (Non-Negotiable)
- Source: Oracle REPT01
- Target: Microsoft Fabric Warehouse
- NO Lakehouses
- NO Notebooks in production pipeline
- Tools allowed: Pipelines + Dataflows + Warehouses + Stored Procedures ONLY
- All connections must be parameterized — never hardcoded
- Use TRUNCATE instead of DROP
- IsActive flag drives what runs (1=active, 0=skip)
- All activities must have descriptions

## Two Main Pipelines
1. PL_Load_Oracle_To_Fabric — Oracle → WH_Target (35 tables)
2. PL_Partner_Data_Sync_And_WaterMark_Refresh — WH_Target → 14 Partner Warehouses

## Data Type Standards (Oracle → Fabric)
- Oracle NUMBER (ID columns) → INTEGER
- Oracle NUMBER (financial/money) → DECIMAL(18,6)
- Oracle DATE (date only) → DATE
- Oracle TIMESTAMP / TLM → DATETIME2
- Oracle VARCHAR2 → NVARCHAR(appropriate size)
- Oracle NUMBER default → DECIMAL(18,6) if unsure

## FilterType Rules
- FilterType = 1: Fact tables — partner filter + watermark
- FilterType = 2: Reference tables — watermark only, no partner filter
- FilterType = else/0: Lookup tables — full copy every run, no filter

## Partner Filter Template (FilterType = 1)
SELECT F.* FROM dbo.[TableName] F
JOIN dbo.T_DW_ACCESS_CONTROL C ON C.PLAN_KEY = F.PLAN_KEY
WHERE C.ACCESS_PARTY_ID = {PartnerId}
AND C.ACTIVE_RECORD_IND = 'Y'

## Watermark Filter Logic
- Watermark fields: TLM or DW_UPD_DTTM or SRC_UPD_TS
- Always use >= (not >)
- Always apply -7 day buffer in watermark SP
- FinalSourceQuery logic:
  FilterType 1: Replace {PartnerId} + append watermark (AND if WHERE exists, else WHERE)
  FilterType 2: Append WHERE watermark only
  FilterType else: No modification

## Naming Conventions
### Pipelines
- PL_[Action]_[Source]_[Destination]
- Examples:
  PL_Load_Oracle_To_Fabric
  PL_Partner_Data_Sync_And_WaterMark_Refresh
  PL_Load_Closure_Enrollment_Weekly

### Activities
- LKP_ = Lookup
- FE_ = ForEach
- CPY_ = Copy Data
- SP_ = Stored Procedure
- SCR_ = Script
- SET_ = Set Variable
- SWT_ = Switch
- IF_ = If Condition

### Stored Procedures
- SP_Load_[TableName] (individual table SPs)
- SP_Load_ALL_AA2_Tables (master SP)
- SP_Update_WaterMark
- SP_Log_Table_Detail

### Schemas
- dbo = staging (temporary per run)
- [STATE_NAME] = final integrated partner schema (e.g. VIRGINIA, ALASKA)
- staging = temporary landing zone

### Warehouses
- WH_Target = consolidated source warehouse
- WH_Metadata = metadata/config warehouse
- WH_[STATENAME] = partner warehouse (e.g. WH_VIRGINIA)

## SP Template Rules
- Always: TRUNCATE + INSERT (never MERGE)
- Always: TRY/CATCH per table
- Always: Log to Metadata.Log (TableName, StartDate, EndDate, Status, ErrorMessage, InsertedRowCount)
- Always: IF table NOT EXISTS → CREATE + INSERT (first run)
- Always: IF table EXISTS → TRUNCATE + INSERT (subsequent runs)
- One failure must NOT stop other tables
- Schema: [PARTNER_NAME].[SP_Load_TableName]

## Metadata Tables (WH_Metadata)
### Config_Oracle.ConfigETL (Pipeline 1)
Columns: Id, SourceSchemaName, SourceTableName, SourceQuery,
WaterMarkField, WaterMarkValue, PrimaryKey, LoadType,
RefreshFrequency, IsFullLoad, IsActive, LastModifiedDate

### Partner Schema (Pipeline 2 — 5 normalized tables)
- Partner.PartnerMaster: PartnerId, PartnerName, PartnerWarehouseName,
  PartnerStagingSchema, PartnerSchemaName, PartnerConnectionString,
  PartnerWarehouseId, PartnerWorkspaceId
- Partner.ConfigMaster: Id, PartnerId, TableId, WaterMarkValue, IsActive
- Partner.TableDefinition: TableId, TableName, SourceWarehouseId,
  SourceQuery, WaterMarkField, FilterType, PrimaryKey
- Partner.SourceConnection: SourceWarehouseId, SourceWarehouse,
  SourceSchemaName, SourceWarehouseConnectionString, SourceWorkspaceId
- Partner.WaterMark_Config: Id, TableName, WaterMarkField,
  WaterMarkValue, PartnerId (temp — cleared each run)

